// @@@ For any index 'index' in the list, if 'index' is greater or equal to 0 and less or equal to the size of the list, then for all 'i' such that 0 <= i < index, the element at position 'i' in the list is equal to the element at position 'i' in the old list. If the element at position 'index' in the list is null, then the element at position 'index' in the old list is also null.

--------------------
// @@@ For all indices i where 0 <= i < index, if the old value at position i in the list is null, the new value at position i is also null. Otherwise, the new value at position i is equal to the old value at position i.

--------------------
// @@@ For all indices i, if the index is greater than or equal to 0 and less than or equal to the size of the list, the element at this index in the list is either null or equal to the element at this index in the old list.

